      "properties": {
        "text": "# T8: bounded local world\n\nT8 World Budget creates an empty world with a 12 GiB CPU KV archive limit. Connect its world output before generation so the next segment is checked before sampling. The limit excludes model weights, output frames and other ComfyUI tasks.\n\nT8 World Stats reports the archive size and remaining budget, then passes the world to Decode. Default: 832x480, two 5-second segments, INT8 KV and 18 historical latent frames.\n\nSelect your installed model filenames in the three loaders. ComfyUI extra_model_paths.yaml supports custom model folders. The nodes call the model and sampler in this process.\n\nT8 Release Caches clears transient history/decoder caches; it does not erase CPU worlds cached by ComfyUI. To free the CPU archive, reset the Drive session or clear the workflow execution cache.\n\nPixelUMM weights retain the NVIDIA noncommercial research/evaluation license. See NOTICE."
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# T8: bounded local world\n\nT8 World Budget creates an empty world with a 12 GiB CPU KV archive limit. Connect its world output before generation so the next segment is checked before sampling. The limit excludes model weights, output frames and other ComfyUI tasks.\n\nT8 World Stats reports the archive size and remaining budget, then passes the world to Decode. Default: 832x480, two 5-second segments, INT8 KV and 18 historical latent frames.\n\nSelect your installed model filenames in the three loaders. ComfyUI extra_model_paths.yaml supports custom model folders. The nodes call the model and sampler in this process.\n\nT8 Release Caches clears transient history/decoder caches; it does not erase CPU worlds cached by ComfyUI. To free the CPU archive, reset the Drive session or clear the workflow execution cache.\n\nPixelUMM weights retain the NVIDIA noncommercial research/evaluation license. See NOTICE."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "markdown": "# T8: bounded local world\n\nT8 World Budget creates an empty world with a 12 GiB CPU KV archive limit. Connect its world output before generation so the next segment is checked before sampling. The limit excludes model weights, output frames and other ComfyUI tasks.\n\nT8 World Stats reports the archive size and remaining budget, then passes the world to Decode. Default: 832x480, two 5-second segments, INT8 KV and 18 historical latent frames.\n\nSelect your installed model filenames in the three loaders. ComfyUI extra_model_paths.yaml supports custom model folders. The nodes call the model and sampler in this process.\n\nT8 Release Caches clears transient history/decoder caches; it does not erase CPU worlds cached by ComfyUI. To free the CPU archive, reset the Drive session or clear the workflow execution cache.\n\nPixelUMM weights retain the NVIDIA noncommercial research/evaluation license. See NOTICE."
      },
